            "kind": "NO_CODE_CHANGE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "src/psu/PSUSensorMain.cpp",
                    "line": 930,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Being able to change ANY sensor to ANY other units isn't really the flexibility we want.  Your use case seems well defined \"I have a voltage sensor that I know the shut resistor value on, and want to turn it into a current sensor\", lets model that in the config, not just allow any arbitrary unit.  For example, turning this into a humidity value wouldn't work as designed, yet this code makes it possible."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/psu/PSUSensorMain.cpp",
                    "line": 930,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "I've resolved the conflicts. Next, I'll work on adding ShuntResistorInOhms support and upload an updated revision afterward.\nThanks."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/psu/PSUSensorMain.cpp",
                    "line": 930,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/psu/PSUSensorMain.cpp",
                    "line": 930,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Overall doesn't look resolved.  This now allows putting a shunt resistor in places that don't make sense.  Left a comment on the specific line that's missing the check."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/psu/PSUSensorMain.cpp",
                    "line": 930,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "Added a voltage-units guard before the shunt resistor logic. Sensor won't be created on mismatch so misconfigurations are easier to spot."
                }
