                    },
                    "message": "Friendly reminder for review, as this change has been waiting for almost a month. Thanks!"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/psu/PSUSensorMain.cpp",
                    "line": 1034,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Do we need a check here that units were Volts prior to this?  Converting a fan tach to an amp sensor with a shunt makes no sense and won't result in these units?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/psu/PSUSensorMain.cpp",
                    "line": 1034,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for the feedback.\nAgreed, converting non-voltage sensors makes no sense. Added a voltage-units guard at the top of the shunt block that rejects and skips the sensor, consistent with other config error handling here. Also added continue in the catch block to match the same pattern.\nLet me know if you'd prefer to just ignore the key and still create the sensor instead."
                }
